  "messages": [
    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Choose one next planning step using the local decision below. Return exactly one listed statement and stop. No other planning choices have been supplied.\n{\"context\": \"A help list records brief questions; the steward can give short consultations while members continue other safe parts of their projects.\", \"decision\": \"How should requests for project help be handled?\", \"goal\": \"Help members make steady progress while sharing tools, work surfaces, materials, and responsibility for the studio.\", \"problem\": \"A neighborhood craft studio serves members working on small personal projects. It has bookable benches, ordinary hand tools, shared consumables, a drying rack, labeled storage, a message board, and a steward during opening hours. Members follow the same basic safety rules. Helpers can support brief activities without taking over the whole room, and each decision concerns a separate routine.\"}\nCANDIDATE STATEMENTS:\nMembers add project questions to the help list, and the steward visits them in the order recorded. A visible queue makes the next consultation predictable while members continue work that does not require assistance.\nThe steward collects project questions during regular bench rounds and answers each brief question at that bench. Members can prepare their questions for the next round instead of monitoring a separate consultation queue.\nMembers mark their project questions by topic on the help list, and the steward gathers people with related questions. A shared explanation can resolve several similar difficulties within one short consultation."
    }
  ],
